  "full_response": "Content delivery networks (CDNs) greatly improve web performance by distributing content across multiple servers and geolocations. This speeds up content delivery and reduces latency, ensuring faster loading times, a crucial factor in user retention and satisfaction. When a user requests a website or resource, the CDN serves it from the closest server, resulting in decreased overall loading time. By caching content on a variety of servers globally, CDNs can heavily reduce the strain on a website’s primary server and spread traffic, making the website more scalable and resilient in the face of high traffic. In addition, CDNs often include advanced security features, feature compression and optimization technologies, and custom configurations that are specific to the needs of the website or content, a further boosting of performance. Overall, by reducing latency, distributing the hosting workload, and optimizing the website, CDNs ensure superior web-performance that translates to increased engagement, better SEO results, and overall improved user experience.",
